research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-12299-- **The converse direction is fine.** A convergent sequence in $\mathbb{R}^{n}$ does have bounded coordinate sequences, each coordinate sequence being convergent by [[thm-componentwise-convergence-and-completeness]] clause 1 and a convergent real sequence being bounded ([[lem-convergent-implies-bounded]]). Only the direction asserted above fails.
